  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Description":          "Audio Scene Manager: acquires audio, edits it into Objects, composes Objects into a Scene, and delivers the Scene. Acquisition and delivery ARE SubAIMs here, unlike in MMC-AMQ and MMC-TST, and legitimately: CAE-AOA and CAE-ASD sit at a HARDWARE boundary, and their consumer is the LISTENER - a person in a dome or wearing headphones - not the User Agent. The Audio Scene Descriptors leave separately, from CAE-ASE, because they are data flowing back to the User Agent's windows while the audio is a rendering leaving the system for a human ear. BASIC AND FULL ARE EXPLICIT throughout: an Object or a Scene of either kind has its own Port, in and out, because the executor routes by Data Type. Each user action is one User Command on a Command Port, so an interactive session is a sequence of runs with the state between them in Shared Storage.",

